# Line endings, pinned.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# docker/entrypoint.sh with CRLF. The file still looks fine in an editor, but
# inside the Linux container `set -e\r` is not a flag and the container dies at
# startup with "set: Illegal option -". Everything that is read by a shell, a
# container, or a container runtime therefore stays LF regardless of platform.

# LF everywhere, in the repository *and* in the working tree. Prettier's
# endOfLine default is "lf", so a CRLF checkout makes `prettier --check` fail on
# files nobody touched — and the pre-commit hook then rewrites whole files as
# pure line-ending churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary, so git never inspects or converts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Aufgezeichnete Portalseiten sind Belege: byte-identisch lassen, sonst
# normalisiert Git ihnen die Zeilenenden weg, die der Server geschickt hat.
apps/directus/extensions/app/src/shared/statbl/fixtures/*.html -text
